        "eyebrow": "2026 — Stoneware",
        "heading": "Assembly",
        "body": "<p>Assembly begins with one form repeated. Each form is pressed, hollowed and left to stiffen, then scored, slipped and joined to the next — a grid built up row by row until it stands on its own.</p><p>The face arrives later. Nothing about a stack of spheres suggests one, until the facial features go on and then it is impossible to see anything else. That turn is the piece.</p><p>The two Assembly 01 colorways came off the same forms and the same bench. One went into the glaze fire and came back running with orange; the other stayed in underglaze, speckled and matte. Precision meets unpredictability in clay — the form is decided, the surface is not.</p>",
